    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b68bd0a6-3492-51ca-ac03-4717dff372b8",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}4{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\mid {x}_{1}\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=5 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nThe supplied nullspace can be written as the span of the independent vectors in\n\n$${x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$$\n\nHence $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$, so $A$ is not invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<5$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{5}$. In particular, $\\text{rank}(A)=4$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 5$ is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$.\n\n- Statement $A\\text{ is not invertible}$ is true. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ is false. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 5$; $A\\text{ is not invertible}$ only.",
